ffairs spends  about 400 million dollars annually on  treating PTSD and other mental health  conditions when you take MDMA it floods  the brain with hormones and  neurotransmitters that evoke feelings of  trust and well-being researchers say  this allows patients to re-examine  traumatic memories all the Bears  like any drug MDMA has side effects and  there's a moderate risk of addiction but  it is less harmful than alcohol or  tobacco small nonprofit is funding the  trial as MDMA is not patentable so big  pharmaceutical companies have steered  clear of the treatment as it will not  make them money for sufferers of PTSD  this new treatment could be a lifesaver  if I hadn't gone through this I'd be an  island so Cemetery  I have a stepson and then if it weren't  for this treatment probably would have  been handed the flag off my casket and  somebody would have had to explain to  him why especially knowing that  treatments are available they made it so  that my stepson will get the flag off my  casket when he's old and gray and I'm  old and gray and after I've watched him  fall in love and graduate high school  college get married bounce a grandchild  on my knee those are the things that  this treatment provides for veterans and  everyone rather than a life cut short  [Music]  you
 

